From: Manikanta Mylavarapu <manikanta.mylavarapu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom_scm: ipq5332: pass PAS metadata size

IPQ5332 TrustZone requires the firmware metadata size with the new PAS
initialization command. The WCSS secure PIL driver was backported without
this prerequisite, leaving qcom_mdt_pas_init() on the legacy two-argument
command. CS-06 logs fail at this operation before loading Q6 segments.

Backport the upstream command-availability check to the Linux 6.18 SCM
implementation. Use the size-aware command when supported and retain the
legacy call for older security firmware. Authentication is unchanged.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260803-rproc-v14-1-a1f87b0b0ad2@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Manikanta Mylavarapu <manikanta.mylavarapu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Gokul Sriram Palanisamy <gokul.sriram.p@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -663,6 +663,14 @@ int qcom_scm_pas_init_image(u32 pas_id, const void *metadata, size_t size,
 
 	desc.args[1] = mdata_phys;
 
+	if (__qcom_scm_is_call_available(__scm->dev, QCOM_SCM_SVC_PIL,
+					 QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_INIT_IMAGE_V2)) {
+		desc.cmd = QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_INIT_IMAGE_V2;
+		desc.arginfo = QCOM_SCM_ARGS(3, QCOM_SCM_VAL, QCOM_SCM_RW,
+					     QCOM_SCM_VAL);
+		desc.args[2] = size;
+	}
+
 	ret = qcom_scm_call(__scm->dev, &desc, &res);
 	qcom_scm_bw_disable();
 
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h
@@ -105,6 +105,7 @@ int qcom_scm_shm_bridge_enable(struct device *scm_dev);
 #define QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_SHUTDOWN	0x06
 #define QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_IS_SUPPORTED	0x07
 #define QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_MSS_RESET	0x0a
+#define QCOM_SCM_PIL_PAS_INIT_IMAGE_V2	0x1a
 
 #define QCOM_SCM_SVC_IO			0x05
 #define QCOM_SCM_IO_READ		0x01
